{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Landed as Gerrit change 1644 (MERGED), commit 746c1ba2e9 on origin/main, with LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1.\n\nCI iteration found four REAL failures (no flakes, so no recheck was warranted): (1) the new dispatcher arm needed a row in docs/exit-codes.md (held-out conformance test) — codes verified against actual CLI behavior first (missing args -> 2, bad SHA -> 1, nothing recorded); (2) four pre-existing store tests attached placeholder SHAs ('a','b','s1','x') that the new seam validation correctly rejects — given real SHAs while preserving their union/dedup/compaction assertions; (3) reducing _completion_precheck 17->16 to satisfy the shrink-only complexity ratchet left the committed baseline STALE, which a test asserts against — drained with --update-stale; (4) attach_commits advertises an outputSchema and had to be classified in tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_output_schema_coverage.py. Reproducing CI's exact selection locally (-m 'not integration and not external' under xdist) was what caught (4): 12128 passed, 0 failed after the fix.\n\nSubmit initially 409'd on a textual conflict Gerrit could not auto-rebase (another agent landed the MCP write-ack {result, push_status} change in _mcp_writes.py and the same coverage test). Resolved by hand keeping BOTH sides — main's new ack wording plus this ticket's attach_commits entry — then re-verified and re-pushed.\n\nTwo notes worth carrying forward: the close gate correctly refused the first close attempt because file_impact was edited after the review (box ticks are exempt, a file_impact edit is material), so a fresh review-plan was required — the gate behaved exactly as documented. And this ticket now records its own landed commit via the very verb it shipped (commits: 746c1ba2e9), which is the feature demonstrating itself end-to-end."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786530789753612001,"uuid":"eea95d57-826d-48c4-b629-2f14af232eda"}